seed_all(SEED)\n","\n","# Make cuDNN use deterministic algorithms when possible\n","torch.backends.cudnn.deterministic = True\n","\n","# Disable cuDNN's automatic algorithm benchmarking\n","torch.backends.cudnn.benchmark = False\n","\n","# Force PyTorch to use deterministic algorithms where supported\n","# warn_only=True gives a warning instead of stopping if an operation\n","# has no deterministic implementation\n","torch.use_deterministic_algorithms(True, warn_only=True)\n","\n","print(\"Random seed:\", SEED)"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":3,"id":"ab2ab6c1","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-08T03:53:51.565058Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-08T03:53:51.564582Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-08T03:53:51.570953Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-08T03:53:51.570044Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.018947,"end_time":"2026-11-08T03:53:51.573088+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-08T03:53:51.554141+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["PyTorch version: 2.11.0+cpu\n","CUDA available: False\n","Using device: cpu\n"]}],"source":["import torch\n","\n","print(\"PyTorch version:\", torch.__version__)\n","print(\"CUDA available:\", torch.cuda.is_available())\n","\n","DEVICE = torch.device(\"cuda:0\" if torch.cuda.is_available() else \"cpu\")\n","\n","print(\"Using device:\", DEVICE)\n","\n","if torch.cuda.is_available():\n","    print(\"GPU:\", torch.cuda.get_device_name(0))"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"808f3b62","metadata":{"_cell_guid":"b1076dfc-b9ad-4769-8c92-a6c4dae69d19","_uuid":"8f2839f25d086af736a60e9eeb907d3b93b6e0e5","papermill":{"duration":0.009234,"end_time":"2026-11-08T03:53:51.59146+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-08T03:53:51.582226+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["# Tokenization\n","\n","Tokenization is one of the most fundamental concepts in Natural Language Processing (NLP) and Large Language Models (LLMs). Before an LLM such as GPT, Gemini, or Claude can understand and process your prompt, it must convert your text into a sequence of tokens.\n","\n","A token can represent:\n","\n","- An entire word.\n","- Part of a word.\n","- A single character.\n","- Punctuation.\n","- Whitespace or other text fragments.\n","\n","The most important thing to understand is that an LLM does not directly process human readable sentences. It processes numerical representations of tokens.\n","\n","Tokenization is the process of breaking text into smaller units called tokens.\n","\n","For example, consider this sentence:\n","\n","```\n","The cat sat on the mat because it was tired.\n","```\n","\n","A simple word-based tokenizer might produce:\n","\n","```\n","['The', 'cat', 'sat', 'on', 'the', 'mat', 'because', 'it', 'was', 'tired', '.']\n","```\n","\n","Another tokenizer might produce:\n","\n","```\n","['The', ' cat', ' sat', ' on', ' the', ' mat', ' because', ' it', ' was', ' tired', '.']\n","```\n","\n","Notice that the second tokenizer preserves spaces as part of tokens.\n","\n","A subword tokenizer might produce something like this.\n","\n","For another sentence:\n","\n","```\n","Tokenization is important.\n","```\n","\n","A tokenizer could produce:\n","\n","```\n","[\"Token\", \"ization\", \" is\", \" important\", \".\"]\n","```\n","\n","Here, `Tokenization` is divided into two pieces:\n","\n","- `Token`\n","- `ization`\n","\n","Why?\n","\n","> Because modern LLMs commonly use subword tokenization. They don't necessarily need a separate vocabulary entry for every possible word.\n","\n","**Is tokenization case-sensitive?**\n","\n","| Tokenizer | Case-sensitive? |\n","|---|---|\n","| bert-base-uncased | No |\n","| bert-base-cased | Yes |\n","| GPT-2 | Yes |\n","\n","## Why do we need tokenization?\n","\n","Imagine you send this prompt to an LLM:\n","\n","```\n","The cat sat on the mat because it was tired.\n","```\n","\n","A computer does not inherently understand the meaning of this English sentence.\n","\n","It needs a numerical representation.\n","\n","The process looks like this:\n","\n","1. Human-readable input: `The cat sat on the mat because it was tired.`\n","2. Tokenization\n","    - Tokens: `['The', 'cat', 'sat', 'on', 'the', 'mat', 'because', 'it', 'was', 'tired', '.']`\n","3. Token-to-ID conversion\n","    - Token IDs: `[22, 24, 32, 31, 28, 25, 50, 30, 29, 34, 1]`\n","4. Embedding layer\n","5. Numerical vectors: Each token ID is mapped to an embedding vector.\n","6. Transformer model: Attention, neural network layers, and prediction.\n","\n","Why is this useful?\n","\n","1. Computers can efficiently process numerical data.\n","2. Tokenization creates a manageable vocabulary.\n","3. Subword tokenization handles unfamiliar words.\n","4. It allows the model to learn patterns between language units.\n","5. It makes language processing compatible with neural networks.\n","\n","## Different types of tokenization\n","\n","There are several tokenization techniques. Let's understand each one.\n","\n","### Word based tokenization\n","\n","This method divides text into individual words.\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":4,"id":"8dcea9f2","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-08T03:53:51.724854Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-08T03:53:51.7245Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-08T03:53:51.72901Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-08T03:53:51.728158Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.016819,"end_time":"2026-11-08T03:53:51.730753+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-08T03:53:51.713934+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[],"source":["text = \"The cat sat on the mat because it was tired.\""]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":5,"id":"57ab8ff8","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-08T03:53:51.750536Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-08T03:53:51.750188Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-08T03:53:55.110936Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-08T03:53:55.109747Z"},"papermill":{"duration":3.373449,"end_time":"2026-11-08T03:53