,"         [ 0.9532,  0.1820, -0.3536,  0.0888, -1.2237],\n","         [ 0.0033, -0.0851, -1.9394,  0.2230, -1.1001],\n","         [ 0.3727, -0.1357, -1.0906, -0.1479,  0.0158],\n","         [ 0.3732, -0.0387, -1.2542,  0.2057, -0.6476],\n","         [-0.3304, -0.2269, -1.8641,  0.5639,  0.6598],\n","         [ 1.2902, -0.1603, -0.5344,  2.0278, -1.1085],\n","         [ 0.4220,  0.0731,  0.1907,  0.4834, -1.2710]]],\n","       grad_fn=<ViewBackward0>)\n"]}],"source":["print(f\"\\nQuery: {W_q} Shape: {Q.shape}\")\n","print(Q)\n","\n","print(f\"\\nKey: {W_k} Shape: {K.shape}\")\n","print(K)\n","\n","print(f\"\\nValue: {W_k} Shape: {V.shape}\")\n","print(V)"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"003ae19e","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.011375,"end_time":"2026-11-08T03:54:17.613758+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-08T03:54:17.602383+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["Important distinction: Q, K, and V are generated for every token, not just one token.\n","\n","So for three tokens, we have:\n","\n","- Three Query vectors.\n","- Three Key vectors.\n","- Three Value vectors.\n","\n","Every token have a Q, K, V value.\n","\n","## Calculate Relationship\n","\n","Now comes the actual attention mechanism. Let's say we want to calculate how much the token `cat` should pay attention to other tokens.\n","\n","Its Query vector is compared against the Key vectors of:\n","\n","- The\n","- cat\n","- sat\n","\n","The comparison is performed using the dot product.\n","\n","The formula is:\n","\n","$$ Scores = QK^T $$\n","\n","Let's understand the dimensions.\n","\n","$$ Q: 3 \\times 4 $$\n","\n","$$ K^T: 4 \\times 3 $$\n","\n","Therefore:\n","\n","$$ QK^T: 3 \\times 3 $$\n","\n","This produces an attention score matrix.\n","\n","For example:\n","\n","$$ Scores = \\begin{bmatrix} 5 & 2 & 1\\\\\\ 2 & 8 & 4\\\\\\ 1 & 4 & 6 \\end{bmatrix} $$"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":60,"id":"d5e6d277","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-08T